Package: oaxaca-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 oaxaca-session,
 oaxaca-shell (= ${binary:Version}),
 oaxaca-themes (= ${binary:Version}),
 oaxaca-config (= ${binary:Version}),
 oaxaca-tools (= ${binary:Version}),
 oaxaca-fonts,
 asdcontrol,
 hyprland-preview-share-picker,
 localsend,
 nwg-displays (>= 0.4.3),
 ffmpegthumbnailer,
 ${port:Depends}
Suggests: oaxaca-desktop-apps, oaxaca-hw-legion, nvtop
Description: Oaxaca desktop (metapackage)
 The whole desktop: the session layer, the shell, the themes, the
 configuration, the command-line tools and the fonts, plus every
 application and utility Omarchy's package list names that Ubuntu's
 archive carries, under the Ubuntu names. The list is read at build time
 from install/oaxaca-base.packages in the ported Omarchy tree, so the
 dependency list and the tree stay in step.
 .
 No web browser is included: Ubuntu's browser packages are snap
 placeholders, and the distro keeps snapd out. "oaxaca-install-browser"
 installs Chrome, Firefox, Brave or Edge from the vendor's own apt source.

Package: oaxaca-tools
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 gum, jq, git, perl, python3, fzf, ripgrep, fd-find, bat,
 hyprland, uwsm, wl-clipboard, grim, slurp, hyprland-guiutils, hyprpicker,
 hyprsunset, xdg-terminal-exec, xdg-utils, xdg-user-dirs,
 desktop-file-utils, libglib2.0-bin, imagemagick, playerctl, brightnessctl,
 pamixer, qrencode, zbar-tools, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-eng, socat,
 wtype, udiskie, pciutils, usbutils
Conflicts: fdclone
Description: Oaxaca command-line tools
 The oaxaca-* commands Omarchy's bin/ directory holds, ported from
 pacman to apt: theme switching, screenshots and recordings, the menu and
 notification helpers, hardware detection, the update pipeline, the
 security setup for fingerprint readers and FIDO2 keys, and the "oaxaca"
 dispatcher that groups them. Also the install-time scripts under
 /usr/share/oaxaca/install that the installer runs on a new system.
 .
 Ubuntu ships fd as fdfind and bat as batcat; this package adds the
 /usr/bin/fd and /usr/bin/bat names the scripts and the shell aliases use.

Package: oaxaca-shell
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 quickshell (>= 0.3.2-0oaxaca2),
 qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-layouts,
 qml6-module-qtquick-shapes, qml6-module-qtquick-effects, qml6-module-qtquick-window,
 qml6-module-qtqml-models,
 oaxaca-config (= ${binary:Version}),
 oaxaca-fonts,
 libxkbcommon-tools
Description: Oaxaca desktop shell (Quickshell)
 The bar, launcher and menu, panels for audio, Bluetooth, network, power
 and brightness, notifications, the lock screen, the screensaver and the
 on-screen display: one Quickshell process loading the plugins under
 /usr/share/oaxaca/shell. The icon font the menu uses for application
 marks comes with it, and so do the Qt QML modules the shell's files import
 (QtQuick with Controls, Layouts, Shapes, Effects and Window, QtQml.Models),
 which Ubuntu's quickshell package only partly depends on.

Package: oaxaca-themes
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Oaxaca theme bundles and templates
 The 22 theme bundles (colour palettes, backgrounds, previews) under
 /usr/share/oaxaca/themes and the templates under
 /usr/share/oaxaca/default/themed that "oaxaca-theme-set" renders
 into the terminal, editor, browser and shell colour files of the active
 theme.

Package: oaxaca-config
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 oaxaca-session,
 oaxaca-tools (= ${binary:Version}),
 oaxaca-themes (= ${binary:Version}),
 hicolor-icon-theme, fontconfig, bluez-tools
Description: Oaxaca configuration and defaults
 Everything that has to be on the system for the desktop to come up: the
 Hyprland configuration and the defaults under /usr/share/oaxaca/default,
 the per-user defaults seeded through /etc/skel, the uwsm and
 environment.d session variables, the fontconfig rules, the systemd user
 units (sleep lock, Bluetooth agent, migration notice, crash watch), the
 system drop-ins (logind), the SDDM theme and
 the Wayland session file, the Plymouth theme files, the application
 launchers and icons, and the branding files.

Package: oaxaca-desktop-apps
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-disk-utility
Description: optional applications for the Oaxaca desktop
 The applications a desktop usually has that nothing in the desktop's own
 scripts or shell needs: GNOME Disks. Installed on request, not by
 oaxaca-desktop, which only suggests it. The document viewer, Papers,
 is part of the desktop itself.
